102. Binary Tree Level Order Traversal

Given the root of a binary tree, return the level order traversal of its nodes' values. (i.e., from left to right, level by level).

Explanation:

FIrst, have a arraylist to store array.
Then have a queue to put all the traversed elements in it, so that as per the numbers in the queue we can traverse its children nodes.
first put the root node in queue.
then hve an array called level to store the children elements.
for every levelkeep adding the array called level to ans;

So take the curr by treenode cur = queue.poll()
this is the element out of queue, add it to the level arr, then check the left and right children nodes, and add them to the q.

fianlly return the nested arrat called ans.


Code:

class Solution {
    public List<List<Integer>> levelOrder(TreeNode root) {
        List<List<Integer>> ans = new ArrayList<>();
        if(root==null){
            return ans;
        }

        Queue<TreeNode> q = new LinkedList<>();
        q.offer(root);
        while(!q.isEmpty()){
            int size = q.size();
            List<Integer> level = new ArrayList<>();

            for(int i=0;i<size;i++){
                TreeNode curr = q.poll();
                level.add(curr.val);

                if(curr.left!=null){
                    q.offer(curr.left);
                }
                if(curr.right!=null){
                    q.offer(curr.right);
                }
            }
            ans.add(level);
        }
        return ans;
    }
}
